HANDLING='Keep tablets or capsules in their supplied packaging, away from children, and follow the pharmacy storage instructions. Do not share medicines or alter the dose yourself. Ask the pharmacy before crushing, opening or dispersing a medicine; formulation-specific instructions differ. Return unused treatment to the pharmacy.'
FERTILITY='Discuss fertility, effective contraception, pregnancy prevention and breastfeeding before treatment. Your team must give the product-specific precautions and duration for you and your partner. Tell oncology promptly about a possible pregnancy.'
WIDER='GIST is a distinct tumour type. A specialist team reviews pathology, KIT/PDGFRA and other relevant molecular findings, prior treatment, symptoms and scans. Surgery may be appropriate for resectable disease or selected situations. Radiotherapy has a selective role, rather than being a routine partner to these tablets. Nutrition, symptom control and supportive or palliative care can be used alongside active cancer treatment.'
GENERIC='Discuss common, serious and lasting effects of targeted therapy, including tiredness, appetite and weight change, nausea or diarrhoea, mouth or skin problems, low blood counts or infection, bleeding, liver or kidney injury, blood-pressure or heart effects, interactions and pregnancy/fertility risks. Some effects can be life-threatening. Each medicine has a different risk pattern; use its separate agent-specific checklist and individualise the conversation.'

def agent(id,name,alias,mechanism,explanation,visual,watch,risks,symptoms):
 return dict(id=id,name=name,alias=alias,type='Oral targeted therapy: tyrosine kinase inhibitor',mechanism=mechanism,explanation=explanation,visual=visual,watch=watch,risks=risks,symptoms=symptoms,source_ids=['nccp',id+'-pi'])
AGENTS={
'imatinib':agent('imatinib','Imatinib','Glivec','Blocks selected growth-signal proteins','Imatinib blocks certain kinase proteins, including KIT and PDGFRA, that can drive susceptible GIST cells. The exact tumour mutation affects sensitivity; a KIT-positive label alone does not replace specialist molecular review. Normal tissues can also be affected.',['Susceptible growth signal','Kinase activity blocked','Cancer growth restrained'],'Report rapid weight gain, swelling, new breathlessness, fever, unusual bleeding, severe rash or yellow eyes promptly. Keep blood tests even if you feel well.',['Nausea, diarrhoea, abdominal discomfort, fatigue, muscle cramps and rash','Swelling around the eyes or elsewhere; occasionally severe fluid retention or heart failure','Low blood counts with infection, anaemia or bleeding','Liver injury, occasionally severe; kidney function may decline with treatment','Rare severe skin reactions, gastrointestinal bleeding or perforation, hepatitis B reactivation and small-vessel clotting that can injure blood cells and kidneys','Fertility or pregnancy harm; discuss product-specific contraception and breastfeeding'],['Fatigue','Nausea','Diarrhoea','Bleeding / bruising','Fever / chills']),
'sunitinib':agent('sunitinib','Sunitinib','Sutent','Blocks growth and blood-vessel signalling','Sunitinib blocks several kinases, including KIT and blood-vessel growth receptors. After imatinib resistance or intolerance it may slow GIST growth. Its effects on normal blood vessels and other tissues explain the need for blood-pressure, heart, thyroid and organ-function monitoring.',['KIT and vessel signals','Several kinases blocked','Tumour growth support reduced'],'Report painful hands or feet, worsening diarrhoea, bleeding, chest pain, breathlessness, faintness, severe headache or a blistering rash promptly. Do not restart after a serious reaction without oncology review.',['Fatigue, appetite or taste change, nausea, diarrhoea and mouth soreness','Painful hand-foot skin reaction, skin or hair colour changes and rash','High blood pressure, thyroid dysfunction and low blood counts','Serious liver injury, heart weakness or rhythm problems, bleeding or blood clots','Rare bowel perforation, pancreatic inflammation, severe skin reactions, neurological syndromes or kidney injury/protein loss, including small-vessel clotting','Impaired wound healing and jaw-bone injury (osteonecrosis); fertility/pregnancy harm','Rare severe infection, low blood glucose or brain effects causing unexplained confusion, seizures or visual change'],['Hand-foot skin reaction','Diarrhoea','Fatigue','Mouth soreness / ulcers','Bleeding / bruising','Nausea']),
'regorafenib':agent('regorafenib','Regorafenib','Stivarga','Blocks several growth and blood-vessel signals','Regorafenib inhibits several kinases that help tumour cells grow and blood vessels support them. In GIST it is used after imatinib and sunitinib. Effects on healthy tissues make skin care, blood-pressure checks and early liver monitoring particularly important.',['Growth and blood-vessel signals','Several kinases blocked','Tumour-supporting signals reduced'],'Report sore hands or feet early. Seek urgent help for yellow eyes, dark urine, severe abdominal pain, significant bleeding, chest pain, breathlessness, severe headache or confusion.',['Hand-foot skin reaction, rash, mouth soreness, fatigue and reduced appetite','Diarrhoea, nausea, vomiting, dehydration and weight loss','High blood pressure and changes in thyroid function','Liver injury, sometimes severe or fatal; frequent early blood tests are essential','Infection, anaemia, low platelets and bleeding; rare heart ischaemia, bowel perforation or abnormal bowel connections (fistulas)','Impaired wound healing and pregnancy harm','Rare severe skin reactions, artery-wall bulging or tearing, small-vessel clotting with kidney injury, or brain effects causing confusion, seizures or visual changes'],['Hand-foot skin reaction','Diarrhoea','Fatigue','Mouth soreness / ulcers','Bleeding / bruising','Nausea'])}

